spec ri04-application-check-vs-edge-insert-lpg: 2 sessions, 6 permutations
# RI04. An application-level RI check: s1 deletes b only if no edge points into it
# (MATCH (b) WHERE NOT ()-->(b) DELETE b); s2 creates a->b. At s1's snapshot b has no
# incoming edge, so the check passes; the native edge RI must still refuse one of the
# two. PostgreSQL without a foreign key permits the orphan.
# Through the lpg API: the check reads InNeighbours in the transaction's view.
# The final dangling probe must count 0 in every permutation: an edge to a dead node
# is never committed (catalogue §9 point 3).

starting permutation: s1d s1c s2e s2c
step s1d: lpg: if InNeighbours(b) is empty, detach-delete b
deleted
-------
1      
(1 row)
step s1c: lpg: Session.EndVersionedTx
step s2e: lpg: AddEdge(a, b)
ERROR: serialization conflict
step s2c: lpg: Session.EndVersionedTx
ERROR: serialization conflict
final final: MATCH (n) RETURN n.name AS name ORDER BY name
name
----
"a" 
(1 row)
final edges: MATCH (x)-[r]->(y) RETURN x.name AS src, r.id AS id, y.name AS dst ORDER BY src, id, dst
src|id|dst
---+--+---
(0 rows)
